== 8.8 Chapter 8 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Pollution is best defined as],
  [the addition of a harmful substance or form of energy],
  [any change in the environment],
  [the loss of habitat],
  [the presence of carbon dioxide]
)

#mcq(2, [Which of these is an air pollutant?],
  [Sulphur dioxide],
  [Humus],
  [Nitrate],
  [Phosphate]
)

#mcq(3, [Carbon dioxide and methane contribute mainly to],
  [the enhanced greenhouse effect],
  [eutrophication],
  [acid rain],
  [ozone depletion]
)

#mcq(4, [CFCs damage the ozone layer because they release],
  [carbon atoms],
  [oxygen],
  [nitrogen atoms],
  [chlorine atoms that break ozone molecules]
)

#mcq(5, [The ozone layer protects life from],
  [gamma rays],
  [ultraviolet radiation],
  [infrared radiation],
  [visible light]
)

#mcq(6, [Acid rain is caused mainly by],
  [CFCs],
  [nitrogen gas],
  [carbon dioxide and methane],
  [sulphur dioxide and nitrogen oxides]
)

#mcq(7, [Eutrophication is caused by],
  [carbon monoxide],
  [noise],
  [nitrate and phosphate enrichment],
  [oil spills]
)

#mcq(8, [Fish die in a eutrophic lake because],
  [decomposers use up the dissolved oxygen],
  [the algae are poisonous],
  [the water is too cold],
  [the water becomes too salty]
)

#mcq(9, [Which step comes first in eutrophication?],
  [Oxygen runs out],
  [Fish die],
  [Plants are shaded out],
  [Algae bloom]
)

#mcq(10, [Oil pollution of water mainly affects birds because it],
  [poisons their food supply only],
  [raises the temperature],
  [destroys the waterproofing of their feathers],
  [increases salinity]
)

#mcq(11, [Deforestation on a hillside leads to],
  [ozone depletion],
  [acid rain],
  [eutrophication],
  [soil erosion]
)

#mcq(12, [Desertification is],
  [the drying of a lake],
  [the formation of a new desert by irrigation],
  [the removal of all plants by fire],
  [the growth of a desert outward or the spread of desert-like conditions]
)

#mcq(13, [Which measure reduces soil erosion on a slope?],
  [Removing all vegetation],
  [Ploughing down the slope],
  [Burning the stubble],
  [Terracing and contour ploughing]
)

#mcq(14, [Conservation is best described as],
  [keeping resources locked away],
  [the wise management of resources for continued use],
  [protecting only animals],
  [maximum exploitation]
)

#mcq(15, [Protecting an organism in its natural habitat is],
  [preservation only],
  [ex situ conservation],
  [in situ conservation],
  [captive breeding]
)

#mcq(16, [A zoo is an example of],
  [a game reserve],
  [in situ conservation],
  [a biosphere reserve],
  [ex situ conservation]
)

#mcq(17, [Yankari National Park is in],
  [Ondo State],
  [Cross River State],
  [Bauchi State],
  [Ogun State]
)

#mcq(18, [A seed bank is an example of],
  [habitat protection],
  [in situ conservation],
  [ex situ conservation],
  [law enforcement]
)

#mcq(19, [Which of these is a renewable resource if managed properly?],
  [Timber],
  [Petroleum],
  [Coal],
  [Natural gas]
)

#mcq(20, [Bush burning is harmful because it],
  [destroys humus and soil organisms],
  [adds too much humus],
  [reduces erosion],
  [increases rainfall]
)

#mcq(21, [The best way to reduce plastic pollution is],
  [dumping it in the sea],
  [burning it in the open],
  [reducing, reusing and recycling],
  [burying it in the garden]
)

#mcq(22, [Which gas causes both acid rain and respiratory disease?],
  [Sulphur dioxide],
  [Methane],
  [Ozone],
  [Helium]
)

#mcq(23, [Thermal pollution from a power station lowers the oxygen in a river because],
  [warm water holds less dissolved oxygen],
  [cold water holds less oxygen],
  [it adds salt],
  [it adds nitrate]
)

#mcq(24, [Afforestation helps a watershed by],
  [raising salinity],
  [destroying humus],
  [reducing erosion and siltation of reservoirs],
  [increasing run-off]
)

#mcq(25, [Which of these is a Nigerian government conservation measure?],
  [Issuing unlimited felling licences],
  [Clearing all forest reserves],
  [Encouraging bush meat trade],
  [Closed seasons and hunting bans]
)

#mcq(26, [A game reserve differs from a national park in that a game reserve],
  [is strictly protected from all human use],
  [may allow controlled hunting],
  [has no wildlife],
  [is always smaller]
)

#mcq(27, [Genetic diversity matters for conservation because it],
  [makes species look different],
  [increases pollution],
  [prevents reproduction],
  [allows populations to adapt to change]
)

#mcq(28, [Which two gases are the main causes of the enhanced greenhouse effect?],
  [Sulphur dioxide and CFCs],
  [Oxygen and nitrogen],
  [Carbon dioxide and methane],
  [Ozone and helium]
)

#mcq(29, [The main cause of ozone depletion is],
  [CFCs from refrigerants and aerosols],
  [methane],
  [carbon dioxide],
  [nitrous oxide]
)

#mcq(30, [Sustainable use means],
  [exporting all resources],
  [using resources no faster than they renew],
  [not using resources at all],
  [using resources as fast as possible]
)

